# nginx-ingress, nginx-agent, affected, high: google.golang.org/grpc v1.81.1 - DoS crash in
# gRPC-Go *xDS servers*. Same package and same root cause as CVE-2026-84304 above; neither NIC
# nor nginx-agent serves xDS, they use grpc as a client between the two.
# FIXED upstream in 1.82.2/1.83.2 - the real fix is bumping NGINX_INGRESS_VERSION (build.env),
# this entry only bridges until that bump lands.
CVE-2026-84445 exp:2026-09-22

# affected, high: libxml2 - stack-based buffer overflow in xmlSnprintfElements
# No fix published by Debian yet (status "affected", no fixed version). libxml2 is a transitive
# package of the NIC base image; the image loads no xslt module and processes no XML or XSLT
# (see misc/config/main_modules.conf), and the affected function is only reached from
# DTD-validation error reporting.
CVE-2026-86140 exp:2026-09-22

# affected, high: libxml2 - double-free/UAF in the libxml2 *Python bindings* (SAX
# attributeDecl callback of python3-libxml2). No fix published by Debian trixie yet. The
# flagged C library is a transitive package of the NIC base image, but the vulnerable path
# only exists with the Python bindings: the image ships neither python3-libxml2 nor any
# Python interpreter (verified: dpkg -l in nginx/nginx-ingress:5.5.4 lists 0 python packages).
CVE-2026-74860 exp:2026-09-22

